tolome-locales (0.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * New locale fon_BJ (Fon, Benin) from the Tolome glossary (LC01-LC26):
    day and month names (Monday first), abbreviations, am_pm zanzan /
    xwelɛkɔ with 24-hour display by default, yes/no words (ɛɛn, eo; whole
    words or y/n, no single-letter shortcut), language name Fɔngbè, country
    name Benɛn, and the 31-letter Fon alphabet for collation (gb, kp and ny
    are letters: a b c d ɖ e ɛ f g gb h i j k l m n o ɔ p kp r s t u v w x y
    ny z). Money, numbers and telephone come from fr_BJ.
  * One more line in i18n/SUPPORTED (fon_BJ.UTF-8 UTF-8); tests/test-fon_BJ.sh
    added; maintainer-script tests now cover both locales.

 -- Anhky <dev@tolome.net>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100

tolome-locales (0.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: locale fr_BJ (French, Benin), compiled with
    localedef --no-archive into /usr/lib/locale.
  * /usr/share/i18n/SUPPORTED is diverted and regenerated by a trigger so
    that Calamares lists the new locales.
  * Structure ready for fon_BJ (one definition file and one manifest line).

 -- Anhky <dev@tolome.net>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
